# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every endpoint, callable without a terminal.
#
#   VS Code    install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), then
#              click the "Send Request" link above any request below.
#   PyCharm /  built in. Click the green arrow in the gutter.
#   IntelliJ
#
# The token: open http://localhost:8080/api/token in a browser tab where you
# are signed in, copy `accessToken` out of the JSON, and paste it below. It is
# good for 15 minutes; when calls start answering 401 with "expired", reload
# that tab and paste a fresh one.
#
# The session cookie is what authenticates that browser tab, which is why the
# token is fetched there rather than here — this client has no session.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@host = http://localhost:5000
@token = PASTE_THE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE


### health — the only endpoint needing no token
GET {{host}}/api/health


### me — identity straight off the token, no network call
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### balance
GET {{host}}/api/tokens/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### check — can the caller afford 1 token?
GET {{host}}/api/tokens/check?amount=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### spend — debits, so it changes state
POST {{host}}/api/tokens/spend
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 1,
  "reason": "manual test"
}


### quote — prices a generation without running it
GET {{host}}/api/generate/quote?references=0&images=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### admin health — 403 unless the token carries the ADMIN role
GET {{host}}/api/admin/health
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### generate — multipart; needs catalogue ids on :8081 and a room photo.
# `rooms` is optional: without it the service falls back to the file at
# ROOM_IMAGE_PATH (assets/room.png), which the repo ships empty, so a request
# with neither answers 503 room_unavailable.
# Answers 202 {jobId}; the generation runs as a job (TASKS_MODE).
# @name generate
POST {{host}}/api/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="prompt"

a modern living room, photorealistic interior
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image_ids"

3,7
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="user_height"

1.70
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="rooms"; filename="room1.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./assets/room1.png
------boundary--


### job status — poll until "done" or "failed"
GET {{host}}/api/jobs/{{generate.response.body.jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### job image — the generated PNG, once the job is done
GET {{host}}/api/jobs/{{generate.response.body.jobId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
